// Regression: two `_` wildcards in one predicate must be INDEPENDENT.
//
// `Login{user: _, server: _}` means "any user, any server" — it must NOT
// require `user == server`. Before the fix, `_` parsed as `Var("_")`, so
// the second `_` equality-checked against the first binding, forcing
// `user == server` and dropping any Login whose user and server differ.
//
// The latent bug was invisible in the corpus because every multi-`_`
// case asserted `count == 0` over traces with no Login at all, so the
// predicate never actually bound. This case has one Login whose
// `user` ("alice") differs from its `server` ("s1"), so a true wildcard
// counts it (n == 1) while the unify-bug would count 0.
def temporal let_(?n, ?A, ?B) {
    exists (?n: Long). (?A == ?n && ?B)
};

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Alert",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    let_(n, count for (t: Timepoint). where (formerly within 1h (Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: _, input.server: _ } && tp(t))), n == 1)};
